ed by the benchmark and gives a later executor a complete handoff without reconstructing behavior from prose.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn scope are the one HTML file's named markup, behavior functions, completion style, browser story, and static handoff verification. Out of scope are all other files, frameworks, persistence, networking, and present-day HTML execution.\n\n## Affected files, systems, data, and interfaces\n\nFuture file: `button-chain.html`. Verification interface: a local browser route. Plan interface: the Markdown artifacts in this directory.\n\n## Dependencies and handoffs\n\nW01 precedes W02; W02 precedes W03; W03 precedes W04. W05 consumes all implementation units. W06 consumes the entire plan and records the final handoff. No external dependency is assumed.\n\n## Implementation approach, risks, and edge cases\n\nUse a stable container and explicit last-button reference. Each click must add one element only; the fourth generated button is a terminal branch and must clear prior content before adding the completion message. Verify no fifth button is added, text is lowercase and exact, and the border is visibly white. Avoid ambiguous counting between the initial button and generated buttons by documenting the chosen count in execution evidence.\n\n## Owned work units\n\nW01–W06 are owned by this goal. Together they cover the markup, two behavior branches, completion style, direct browser acceptance, and static plan handoff.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
