{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/01-button-chain/goal.md; ls basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/01-button-chain/steps\"","aggregated_output":"# Goal 01: button-chain\n\n## Current state and prior-goal handoffs\n\nNo prior goal exists. The plan is a draft for a future standalone HTML implementation; the proof itself has not created or run HTML.\n\n## Outcome and definition of done\n\nDefine an executable, independently reviewable contract for the complete button-chain interaction and its browser acceptance flow. Done when the future executor can create one initial button, append exactly one below the current last button per click, clear on the fourth generated button, show exact `finished` with a visible white border, and run the named checks.\n\n## Why this goal is needed\n\nIt owns the single coherent user-visible outcome required by the benchmark and gives a later executor a complete handoff without reconstructing behavior from prose.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn scope are the one HTML file's named markup, behavior functions, completion style, browser story, and static handoff verification. Out of scope are all other files, frameworks, persistence, networking, and present-day HTML execution.\n\n## Affected files, systems, data, and interfaces\n\nFuture file: `button-chain.html`. Verification interface: a local browser route. Plan interface: the Markdown artifacts in this directory.\n\n## Dependencies and handoffs\n\nW01 precedes W02; W02 precedes W03; W03 precedes W04. W05 consumes all implementation units. W06 consumes the entire plan and records the final handoff. No external dependency is assumed.\n\n## Implementation approach, risks, and edge cases\n\nUse a stable container and explicit last-button reference. Label the initial button `Button 0` and generated buttons `Button 1` through `Button 4` so browser targets are deterministic and accessible. Each click on the current last button must add one element only; after clicks on buttons 0, 1, 2, and 3 have created generated buttons 1–4, pressing generated button 4 is the terminal branch and must clear prior content before adding the completion message. Verify no fifth button is added, text is lowercase and exact, and the border is visibly white.\n\n## Owned work units\n\nW01–W08 are owned by this goal. Together they cover the deterministic markup, two behavior branches, completion style, direct browser acceptance, static plan handoff, validator report, and benchmark analysis report.\n01-step-initial-markup-testing.md\n01-step-initial-markup.md\n02-step-append-behavior-testing.md\n02-step-append-behavior.md\n03-step-completion-behavior-testing.md\n03-step-completion-behavior.md\n04-step-completion-style-testing.md\n04-step-completion-style.md\n05-step-browser-acceptance-testing.md\n05-step-browser-acceptance.md\n06-step-static-handoff-testing.md\n06-step-static-handoff.md\n07-step-validation-report-testing.md\n07-step-validation-report.md\n08-step-analysis-report-testing.md\n08-step-analysis-report.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
