n | 09-step-html-audit |\\n| W10 | verification | `N/A` | `worker process-group cleanup audit` | `N/A` | Confirm no matching browser/server/driver process remains from this worker. | W06 | 01-button-chain | 10-step-process-audit |\\n| W05 | verification | `N/A` | `US-01 button-chain acceptance flow` | `N/A` | Execute the exact five-click browser flow against the future workspace-root file. | W01, W02, W03, W04 | 02-ui-validation | 01-step-browser-acceptance |\\n| W11 | docs | `ui-user-stories.md` | `US-01 result row` | `N/A` | Record the browser story status and evidence without weakening its direct-input contract. | W05 | 02-ui-validation | 02-step-story-result |\\n| W12 | docs | `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` | `US-01 run cache` | `N/A` | Record every click, readiness wait, and actual run result. | W05 | 02-ui-validation | 03-step-story-cache |\\n| W13 | docs | `bugs.md` | `UI bug register` | `N/A` | Preserve any observed bug with investigation, fix, and retest traceability; retain an empty register when none is found. | W05 | 02-ui-validation | 04-step-bug-register |\\n| W08 | docs | `analysis-report.md` | `Benchmark execution report` | `N/A` | Record revision, exact timestamps, elapsed time, worker result, validation/review results, artifact/process audit, thread source, and token evidence. | W05, W07, W09, W10, W11, W12, W13 | 02-ui-validation | 05-step-analysis-report |\\n\\n## Decomposition review\\n\\n- [x] Every definition-of-done item maps to one or more work units.\\n- [x] Every known affected file and changing symbol has its own work unit.\\n- [x] Every work unit has exactly one goal and one step.\\n- [x] Each goal has 2–10 work units, or records an allowed exception.\\n- [x] Each step has exactly one work unit and no unnamed incidental edits.\\n- [x] Dependencies form an executable order with no cycle.\\n--- basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/progress.md\\n# Progress: basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\\n\\n**Overall progress:** `0%  #### ----------------  100%` 💤\\n\\n| Goalname | Description | Completion status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 01-button-chain | Complete the button-chain implementation contract and static safety handoff. | 💤 incomplete |\\n| 02-ui-validation | Execute and record the final browser story and benchmark handoff. | 💤 incomplete |\\n--- basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/bugs.md\\n# UI bugs: basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\\n\\nNo browser execution was permitted in this planning-only proof, so no bug was observed. The required bug feedback loop remains available if US-01 fails during future implementation verification.\\n\\n| ID | Story | Severity | Reproduction/evidence | Investigation goal | Fix goal | Retest story | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n--- basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/context-snapshot.md\\n# Context snapshot: basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\\n\\n## Snapshot time\\n\\n2026-08-10 (Europe/Berlin); exact start and end timestamps are recorded in `analysis-report.md`.\\n\\n## Confirmed context\\n\\n- Workspace: `/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.2.0/workspace`.\\n- Tagged skill: `/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.2.0/source/planning/SKILL.md`.\\n- Relative UI reference read: `/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.2.0/source/planning/references/ui-user-story-validation.md`.\\n- Future artifact: `button-chain.html`; it was not created or inspected.\\n- Session ID is in the workspace root `session-id.txt`, sourced from `CODEX_THREAD_ID`.\\n- Plan remains resumable with two ordered goals and fourteen explicitly owned work units.\\n\\n## Next executor action\\n\\nRead `progress.md`, then `01-button-chain/goal.md`. Create only the named future HTML target, execute its separate verification companions, update story evidence and progress, and rerun the tagged validator.\\n\\n## Handoff and caveats\\n\\nThe decomposition, review draft, story contract, cache, and empty bug register are present. `validation.md` and the final `analysis-report.md` are planned owned deliverables and will be written after the final validator/audits. Browser evidence is intentionally absent and the plan is not execution-complete. No browser, server, driver, or HTML artifact may be started by this proof.\\n--- basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/ui-user-stories.md\\n# UI user stories: basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\\n\\n| ID | Persona / precondition | Browser actions | Interaction evidence | Expected observable result | Status | Evidence | Related work units | Run cache |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| US-01 | A visitor opens the future local `button-chain.html` at its initial state. | Open the local file; click accessible `Button 0`, then `Button 1`, `Button 2`, `Button 3`, and finally `Button 4`. | Mouse click the named visible button after each append. | Each of the first four clicks adds exactly one button below the prior last button; pressing generated `Button 4` clears the document and leaves exact lowercase `finished` with a visible white border. | 💤 untested | Not executed because this proof forbids creating, opening, inspecting, serving, or testing HTML. Future evidence must include route, click sequence, visible button counts, and one decisive screenshot. | W01, W02, W03, W04, W05 | `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` |\\n--- basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/adversarial-review.md\\n# Adversarial review: basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\\n\\n## Review scope\\n\\n- Request: Fresh secondary review of exact task coverage, UI-validation ordering, atomic ownership, deterministic five-click story/cache, testing companions, validator/report/audit scope, bug register, context, progress, and safety boundary.\\n- Repository/context inspected: the isolated plan directory only; `/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.2.0/source/basic-test-proof-plan.md`; `/tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.2.0/source/planning/SKILL.md`; and the required `planning/references/ui-user-story-validation.md`. No HTML, browser, server, driver, or execution tooling was inspected or run.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n| ID | Missing or over-broad item | Required plan change | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| AR-01 | `plan-description.md` still declares `Adversarial review` status `💤 pending`, although this is the final secondary review artifact. | After all findings are resolved, change that status to `✅ approved` in `plan-description.md` to satisfy the planning skill’s required status match. | ⏳ unresolved |\\n| AR-02 | The plan-level `progress.md` lists only `01-button-chain`; the existing `02-ui-validation` goal and its five owned units are absent from the plan tracker. | Add `02-ui-validation` as the ordered final goal with its incomplete status, then keep the tracker synchronized with both goal directories. | ⏳ unresolved |\\n| AR-03 | W01 says it defines generated labels `Button 1`–`Button 4`, while W02 also owns appending the next labelled button. This gives label-definition responsibility to two work units. | Restrict W01 to the initial `Button 0` markup and assign the generated label sequence exclusively to W02 (or create a distinct contract-only target); update the inventory and affected step text consistently. | ⏳ unresolved |\\n| AR-04 | W06’s testing companion asks its validator check to verify mandatory artifacts and perform HTML/process audits, although W07, W09, and W10 separately own those targets. | Limit W06’s companion to validator execution/output; keep artifact and process assertions in the W07/W09/W10 companions so each verification target remains atomic. | ⏳ unresolved |\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\n- Status: `❌ changes required`\\n- Rationale: The five-click story and cache, final UI-goal placement, bug register, context, report/audit intent, testing companions, and safety prohibition are otherwise represented, but the findings above leave status synchronization and work-unit ownership/verification boundaries unresolved.\\n--- /tmp/20260810T121526Z-benchmark8/1.2.0/workspace/basic-test-proof-1.2.0-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/01-button-chain/goal.md\\n# Goal 01: button-chain\\n\\n## Current state and prior-goal handoffs\\n\\nNo prior goal exists. The plan is a draft for a future standalone HTML implementation; the proof itself has not created or run HTML.\\n\\n## Outcome and definition of done\\n\\nDefine an executable, independently reviewable implementation contract and static safety handoff for the button-chain. Done when the future executor can create one initial button, append exactly one below the current last button per click, clear on generated `Button 4`, show exact `finished` with a visible white border, and the tagged validator and safety audits are separately specified.\\n\\n## Why this goal is needed\\n\\nIt owns the single coherent user-visible outcome required by the benchmark and gives a later executor a complete handoff without reconstructing behavior from prose.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nIn scope are the one HTML file's named markup, behavior functions, completion style, tagged validation, HTML artifact audit, and process cleanup audit. Browser story execution and result/report artifacts are owned by final goal 02. Out of scope are all other files, frameworks, persistence, networking, and present-day HTML execution.\\n\\n## Affected files, systems, data, and interfaces\\n\\nFuture file: `button-chain.html`. Verification interface: a local browser route. Plan interface: the Markdown artifacts in this directory.\\n\\n## Dependencies and handoffs\\n\\nW01 precedes W02, W03, and W04. W06, W07, W09, and W10 provide static handoff evidence; the final UI-validation goal consumes the implementation and audit handoffs. No external dependency is assumed.\\n\\n## Implementation approach, risk